WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.2 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
From Theory of Change to results framework

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
A results framework turns your Theory of Change into a table you can monitor from your pilot.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
A results framework turns your Theory of Change into a table. For each external objective it lists the outcomes and outputs you expect, how you will know, and what must hold true.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
What goes in the table

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:38.611
Results chain: Impact, outcomes and outputs, copied from your pathway for the first year. For example: Output 2.1.1: four trainees complete six months. Outcome 2.1: trainees gain baking skills.

6
00:00:38.611 --> 00:00:50.311
Evidence: How you will know each result happened, with data you can actually get. For example: Attendance sheets for the output; a skills checklist and hygiene certificate for the outcome.

7
00:00:50.311 --> 00:01:00.530
Assumptions: What must hold true for one level to lead to the next. For example: Local employers will hire young people who hold a traineeship certificate.

8
00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:11.578
Codes: The labels from your strategy that link results to plans and budgets. For example: ESO2, Outcome 2.1, Output 2.1.1, used the same way everywhere.

9
00:01:11.978 --> 00:01:12.578
Why it matters

10
00:01:12.578 --> 00:01:17.881
1. Funders often ask for a logframe in your first application.

11
00:01:17.881 --> 00:01:23.556
2. It shows whether your plan adds up before you spend money.

12
00:01:23.556 --> 00:01:29.859
3. It keeps your pilot focused on results you can monitor.

13
00:01:30.259 --> 00:01:30.859
What it feeds

14
00:01:30.859 --> 00:01:36.533
1. Your indicators: at least one for each result in the table.

15
00:01:36.533 --> 00:01:41.467
2. Your plans and budget, linked through the same codes.

16
00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:47.770
3. Your monitoring and reports: planned versus actual, result by result.

17
00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:48.770
What to avoid

18
00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:54.815
Copying every box of your diagram, not only what you can monitor.

19
00:01:54.815 --> 00:01:59.748
Claiming you will measure impact in your first year.

20
00:01:59.748 --> 00:02:06.052
Skipping the logic check, upwards and across to real evidence.

21
00:02:06.652 --> 00:02:08.452
You build a results framework for one external objective.

22
00:02:08.452 --> 00:02:12.452
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:13.952 --> 00:02:17.052
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
